<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9389" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνταῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄντα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>set over against, right opposite,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνταία πληγή</span> a wound <i>in
				front, right in the breast,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				195
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				844
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνταίαν ἔπαισεν</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πληγήν</span>) <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1308
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>opposed to, hostile, hateful,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνώδαλον ἀ. βροτοῖσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					588
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πομπά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					1323
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				72
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				334
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεός</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				335
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τἀνταῖα θεῶν</span> their
				<i>hostile purposes,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				604
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>besought with prayers,</i> epith. of Hecate, etc., <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.1141
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>H.</u>
				41.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνταία: . . ἱκέσιος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i>(<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				223
			</span></i>)ap.<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνταῖος Ζεύς</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				22.113
			</span></i>.</div>
